@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+Feature: Source conformance
+  As a maintainer
+  I want the production code to preserve DOM element identity on state toggles
+  So that browser-held references do not become detached on completion-state changes
+
+  @conformance
+  Scenario: The toggleTodo function does not call render
+    Given the source at "js/app.js"
+    When the conformance checker inspects the toggleTodo function
+    Then toggleTodo must not call render
+    And toggleTodo must toggle the completed class on the existing list item node in-place
+
+  @conformance
+  Scenario: The toggle-all handler mutates existing nodes in-place
+    Given the source at "js/app.js"
+    When the conformance checker inspects the toggle-all click handler
+    Then the handler must not call render
+    And the handler must toggle the completed class on each existing list item node in-place
+
+  @conformance
+  Scenario: The render function does not clear and rebuild the entire todo list
+    Given the source at "js/app.js"
+    When the conformance checker inspects the render function
+    Then the render function must not reassign innerHTML on the todo-list element
+    And the render function must not recreate li elements that already exist
